  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v0.3.1 - Hotfix for WAVE_FORMAT_EXTENSIBLE PCM input. AudioConverter previously threw ArgumentException(\"Input must be PCM or IEEE float\") on multi-channel WAVs whose fmt chunk uses formatTag 0xFFFE (the standard format for Windows capture pipelines and most modern DAWs), even when the underlying SubFormat was KSDATAFORMAT_SUBTYPE_PCM with byte-identical PCM samples. Fix: detect the extensible format tag, inspect the SubFormat GUID, and re-label the WaveFormat as standard PCM or IEEE float without converting any bytes. Multi-channel inputs now flow through to MediaFoundationResampler unchanged. Unknown SubFormats raise NotSupportedException with a clear message rather than the misleading downstream resampler error.",
